ntdll: bridge apple's GPTK 4.0b2 D3DMetal into wine 11.14.

Loads libd3dshared.dylib from lib/external, forces its internal enableUnixCall
flag on, wraps the graphics dispatch init so the entries gptk routes through
unix calls are cleared, bridges D3DMetal's native worker threads, and registers
wine's PE mappings with rosetta.

Notes from bringing this up on 4.0b2 specifically:

  - PatchUnixCallTable() must NOT be called from here.  On 4.0b2 it does
    memmove(__wine_unix_call_funcs + 840, NULL, 0x60) and faults.  It carries
    its own dispatch_once token, so gptk invokes it once it is actually ready.
    Kept behind WINE_D3DM_PATCH_MASK bit 2 for comparison.

  - The dispatch entries to clear are gptk's own list, {0, 9, 11, 42, 43} kept
    (mask 0xc0000000a01), read out of the disassembly of D3DRMDispatch_Init:
    it clears exactly those indices itself when enableUnixCall is set, but its
    init resets the flag before that test, so the clearing is redone here.
    This only works after PatchEntrypointCallTable() has grown the unixlib
    table from 9 to 39 entries.

  - The native-thread thunk target lives in the per-module unixlib on 4.0b2
    (whisky symlinks all four names to libd3dshared.dylib), so the owner
    allowlist covers the d3d unixlib names too.

  - wine 11.14 maps DLLs through virtual_map_image(); virtual_map_module() only
    ever sees the main image and virtual_create_builtin_view() is not called at
    all, so the rosetta registration lives in virtual_map_image().

  - Apple's pthread_self() reads the thread pointer from %gs:0x0.  Native code
    called straight from PE therefore needs a valid self pointer there while
    wine's TEB is in %gs; NT_TIB.ExceptionList is unused on x86_64 and carries
    it.  The mach-thread-port slot cannot be mirrored the same way (it would
    land on Tib.SubSystemTib, which wine uses), so direct native calls that
    take an os_unfair_lock still fail -- see D3DMETAL_GS_THUNK, which is the
    groundwork for routing those through a gsbase swap.

  - The apple gsbase restore paths lacked the NULL guard the linux ones have;
    without it a thread whose pthread_teb is not set yet gets gsbase zeroed.

Verified: D3D12CreateDevice reports feature level 12_2 with adapter
"AMD Compatibility Mode", i.e. D3DMetal rather than wine's vkd3d, with no
environment variables set.

